{
  "dom_id": "step-q37510",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Determine the solutions of the equation $10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}x-10{x}^{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(x)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2}x-10{x}^{2} \\\\ 10{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2}x \\\\ 10{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can factor out the $\\frac{x}{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}(20{x}^{2}+24x-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $20{x}^{2}+24x-9$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}(20{x}^{2}+24x-9) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}(10x-3)(2x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=\\frac{3}{10},$ and $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
